  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## Highlights\n\n### Custom syntax themes for code blocks\n\n- Register arbitrary TextMate `IRawTheme` instances with `SyntaxHighlighting.RegisterCustomTheme`.\n- Select a registered theme through:\n  - `CodeBlock.CustomColorTheme`\n  - `MarkdownRenderer.CodeBlockCustomColorTheme`\n- Existing `ColorTheme` remains fully supported as the built-in fallback.\n- Unregistered custom theme names also fall back to `ColorTheme`.\n- Added parsed-theme and color-brush caching to reduce repeated highlighting overhead.\n- Added `SyntaxHighlighting.UnregisterCustomTheme`.\n\n### Inherited renderer properties\n\n`ColorTheme`, `CustomColorTheme`, and `LinkContextMenu` are now inherited Avalonia properties.\n\nThis keeps the existing renderer-level API while allowing individual code blocks or text blocks to override the inherited value through a local value or style.\n\n### More reliable streaming rendering\n\n- `MarkdownRenderer.ArrangeCore` remains synchronous.\n- Markdown parsing is serialized through a single render task.\n- Stale parse results are discarded using builder identity and version checks.\n- Pending renders are cancelled when the renderer is detached or its builder is replaced.\n- Prevents outdated asynchronous results from overwriting newer content.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nExisting `CodeBlock.ColorTheme` usage remains unchanged.\n\nCustom theme names use exact matching and must not conflict with built-in `ThemeName` values.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/DearVa/LiveMarkdown.Avalonia/compare/v2.2.2...v2.3.0",
